---
const symptoms = [
  'Design calls it copy.',
  'Product calls it onboarding friction.',
  'Support calls it tickets.',
  'Engineering calls it edge cases.',
  'Customer Success calls it repeated explanation.',
  'Leadership calls it activation, conversion, or data-quality risk.',
];
---
<section id="recognition">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-label">Recognition</div>
    <h2>Your team may already be naming the symptom wrong.</h2>
    <div class="symptom-strip" aria-label="Common labels for the same guidance failure">
      {symptoms.map((symptom) => <span class="symptom-chip">{symptom}</span>)}
    </div>
    <p class="problem-interpretation">They may all be paying for the same failure from different budgets: the product asks the user to continue before the next move has been made legible.</p>
    <p class="section-copy recognition-close">That is where the review begins.</p>
  </div>
</section>
